V3DRender 0.10: kit 12, recovering after a failed run
=====================================================

0.10 adds a way out when something has gone wrong:

  *V3DReset       ends every GPU job (running or waiting) and resets
                  the GPU; programs waiting on them are told they failed
  *V3DReset all   the same, and closes every V3DRender file left open
                  by programs that stopped without closing (Alt-Break,
                  an error); any program still using the GPU must start
                  again

V3DRender also now resets a job that has run for 5 seconds even if it
keeps moving (before, only one that stopped moving for 0.5 s).

HangTest has a new test 10: a job that never ends with a frame queued
behind it, both ended at once by the reset, and the GPU working after.
Check (tests 1-8) runs as before on 0.10. The buffer area is still
256 MB unless set (*RMLoad V3DRender Size <MB>).

Before you start
- A Pi 4, Pi 400 or CM4 with RISC OS 5.30 or later. V3DDriver not
  loaded. Copy this folder to a hard disc.

The test
1. Double-click Replay. It loads V3DRender 0.09 from this folder, in
   place of an older one. No program should be using the GPU at the same time:
   Replay needs the buffer addresses Mesa's job had.
2. Optional: double-click Check too (kits 1-5's tests, all passed in
   kit 5).
3. Send Results back.
